---
// Three privacy cards, each with a small live vignette of the app.
const rows3 = [
  {
    sentence: "AI sorting",
    on: "Sends sender, subject and preview to the provider you chose.",
    off: "Nothing leaves this machine for sorting.",
    checked: false,
  },
  {
    sentence: "Agent access (MCP)",
    on: "Granted clients may read and archive, each account you allow.",
    off: "Local agents cannot reach your mail.",
    checked: false,
  },
];
---
<section class="priv wrap" id="privacy">
  <h2 class="h2" data-reveal>Private by design</h2>
  <p class="lead" data-reveal style="--i:1">
    Your mail lives in one encrypted database on your disk. There is no Emc²
    server and no cloud copy.
  </p>
  <div class="priv-cards">
    <article class="pcard" data-reveal>
      <div class="vig" data-ui>
        <div class="switch-row on" data-band>
          <span class="switch-text">
            <span class="switch-s">Encrypt mail on disk</span>
            <span class="switch-c" data-on="Mail.db is encrypted; the key never leaves the keychain." data-off="Mail.db is encrypted; the key never leaves the keychain.">Mail.db is encrypted; the key never leaves the keychain.</span>
          </span>
          <button class="toggle" type="button" aria-checked="true" aria-disabled="true" aria-label="Encrypt mail on disk"><i /></button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3>Encrypted on disk</h3>
      <p>Mail is stored encrypted with a key your system keychain protects. If encryption is unavailable, Emc² stops instead of saving plain text.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="pcard" data-reveal style="--i:1">
      <div class="vig" data-ui>
        <div class="conn">
          <i class="acct-dot" />
          imap.fastmail.com
          <small>TLS · Direct</small>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3>No server in between</h3>
      <p>The app talks straight to Gmail or your IMAP server. Nothing is copied to a cloud of ours, because there isn't one.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="pcard" data-reveal style="--i:2">
      <div class="vig" data-ui>
        {rows3.map((band) => (
          <div class={`switch-row${band.checked ? " on" : ""}`} data-band>
            <span class="switch-text">
              <span class="switch-s">{band.sentence}</span>
              <span class="switch-c" data-on={band.on} data-off={band.off}>{band.checked ? band.on : band.off}</span>
            </span>
            <button class="toggle" type="button" aria-checked={band.checked ? "true" : "false"} aria-label={band.sentence}><i /></button>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <h3>AI and agents stay off</h3>
      <p>
        AI sorting uses a key you add: OpenAI, or TypeSafe's Jev model through TypeSafe, OpenRouter or Vercel AI
        Gateway. Local agent access (MCP) is off by default, and sending needs its own opt-in.
      </p>
      <p class="payload-cap">Each new message, as Jev receives it:</p>
      <pre class="payload"><code>From: priya@studio-north.com
Subject: Can we move Thursday's review?

Something came up on my side. Does Friday at 10:00 work instead?</code></pre>
      <p class="payload-note">OpenAI also receives the cached message content and metadata</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
